{"type":"message","id":"33b45d58","parentId":"75158c26","timestamp":"2026-05-18T11:26:19.724Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_CIDSkQ3kcCi1tJVZq65niCtv","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"set -e\ncurl -L -sS --max-time 30 'https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/' -o /tmp/coindesk.xml\ncurl -L -sS --max-time 30 'https://cointelegraph.com/rss' -o /tmp/ct.xml\ncurl -L -sS --max-time 30 'https://decrypt.co/feed' -o /tmp/decrypt.xml\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\nfor name,path in [('CoinDesk','/tmp/coindesk.xml'),('CoinTelegraph','/tmp/ct.xml'),('Decrypt','/tmp/decrypt.xml')]:\n    print('\\n##',name)\n    txt=open(path,'rb').read()\n    root=ET.fromstring(txt)\n    for item in root.findall('.//item'):\n        title=(item.findtext('title') or '').strip()\n        if any(k in title.lower() for k in ['bitcoin', 'btc', 'crypto', 'liquid', 'selloff', 'iran']):\n            pub=(item.findtext('pubDate') or '').strip()\n            link=(item.findtext('link') or '').strip()\n            desc=(item.findtext('description') or '').strip()\n            print('TITLE:',title)\n            print('PUB:',pub)\n            print('LINK:',link)\n            print('DESC:',desc[:300])\n            print('---')\nPY","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher","timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","usage":{"input":4832,"output":1102,"cacheRead":49792,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55726,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779103570730,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DgqOtnCX3aYE2F5HhCZ8tUSsVBoEF"}}
{"type":"message","id":"bc1ff6dc","parentId":"33b45d58","timestamp":"2026-05-18T11:26:22.300Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_CIDSkQ3kcCi1tJVZq65niCtv","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## CoinDesk\nTITLE: The three risks that could overwhelm bitcoin's regulatory tailwind\nPUB: Mon, 18 May 2026 11:08:19 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/daybook-us/2026/05/18/the-three-risks-that-could-overwhelm-bitcoin-s-regulatory-tailwind\nDESC: Your day-ahead look for May 18, 2026\n---\nTITLE: Bitcoin slides below $77,000 as Trump’s Iran warning rattles risk assets\nPUB: Mon, 18 May 2026 10:50:13 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/bitcoin-slides-below-usd77-000-as-trump-s-iran-warning-rattles-risk-assets\nDESC: Bitcoin and ether sank after the U.S. president told Iran the “clock is ticking,” sending oil higher and triggering broad crypto liquidations.\n---\nTITLE: Fed minutes, Meta stablecoin Senate deadline: Crypto Week Ahead\nPUB: Mon, 18 May 2026 10:36:34 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/fed-minutes-meta-stablecoin-senate-deadline-crypto-week-ahead\nDESC: Your look at what's coming in the week starting May 18.\n---\nTITLE: Crypto security is turning into an AI arms race as agents may overwhelm compliance teams\nPUB: Mon, 18 May 2026 07:13:08 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2026/05/18/crypto-security-is-turning-into-an-ai-arms-race-as-agents-may-overwhelm-compliance-teams\nDESC: AI agents and automated payments could reach a scale that crypto monitoring systems built for human-paced markets cannot handle, Elliptic CEO Simone Maini warned.\n---\nTITLE: Bitcoin Depot, North America's largest bitcoin ATM operator, files for bankruptcy\nPUB: Mon, 18 May 2026 06:55:50 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/bitcoin-depot-once-north-america-s-largest-bitcoin-atm-operator-files-for-bankruptcy\nDESC: Bitcoin Depot, the largest bitcoin ATM operator in North America and publicly listed on Nasdaq, has filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy.\n---\nTITLE: Iran may be turning the Strait of Hormuz into a bitcoin-based insurance market, local reports say\nPUB: Mon, 18 May 2026 06:47:37 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/iran-may-be-turning-the-strait-of-hormuz-into-a-bitcoin-insurance-market-local-reports-say\nDESC: State-linked Fars News reported that Iran’s economy ministry has been working on a plan to manage shipping through the Strait with payments in bitcoin.\n---\nTITLE: Crypto traders betting on a rally lose $563 million in liquidations. Ether and bitcoin suffer the most\nPUB: Mon, 18 May 2026 05:47:13 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/crypto-traders-betting-on-a-rally-lose-usd563-million-in-liquidations-ether-and-bitcoin-suffer-the-most\nDESC: Ether and bitcoin led liquidations, as their prices dropped on macroeconomic concerns.\n---\nTITLE: HYPE pops 7%, beating bitcoin declines, as SpaceX pre-IPO lands on Hyperliquid\nPUB: Mon, 18 May 2026 05:01:11 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/hype-pops-7-beating-bitcoin-declines-as-spacex-pre-ipo-lands-on-hyperliquid\nDESC: Hyperliquid's HYPE token rallied 7% over 24 hours after Trade.xyz launched the first pre-IPO perpetual market on the platform, offering synthetic exposure to SpaceX at a reference valuation of $1.78 trillion.\n---\nTITLE: Yet another crypto bridge falls victim to an $11 million hack\nPUB: Mon, 18 May 2026 04:37:06 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/yet-another-crypto-bridge-falls-victim-to-an-usd11-million-hack\nDESC: The latest attack adds to growing string of cross-chain infrastructure exploits.\n---\nTITLE: Bitcoin slides under $77,000 as oil shock and Treasury yields hit risk assets\nPUB: Mon, 18 May 2026 03:52:10 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/bitcoin-slides-under-usd77-000-as-oil-shock-and-treasury-yields-hit-risk-assets\nDESC: Long-term holders are still sitting tight and exchange balances remain near six-year lows, Binance Research data shows, but underwater short-term holders leave BTC vulnerable to macro shocks.\n---\nTITLE: The Clarity Act took a step forward: State of Crypto\nPUB: Sun, 17 May 2026 18:30:00 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/17/the-clarity-act-took-a-step-forward-state-of-crypto\nDESC: Unpacking Thursday's at-times contentious markup hearing.\n---\nTITLE: DeFi's new front: VerifiedX bets bitcoin's next chapter is programmable, private\nPUB: Sun, 17 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2026/05/17/defi-s-new-front-verifiedx-bets-bitcoin-s-next-chapter-is-programmable-private\nDESC: VerifiedX says its Bitcoin sidechain enables programmable, privacy-preserving transactions without synthetic wrappers, targeting growing institutional demand for native DeFi on the original blockchain system.\n---\nTITLE: Japan's SBI Securities, Rakuten Securities plan to offer crypto investment trusts\nPUB: Sun, 17 May 2026 11:41:31 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/05/17/japan-s-sbi-securities-rakuten-securities-plan-to-offer-crypto-investment-trusts\nDESC: Another 11 companies responded to a survey saying they would consider offering crypto funds once the regulatory environment becomes clear.\n---\nTITLE: Jump Crypto’s ‘Firedancer’ is taking a slow and steady approach to its long-awaited Solana infrastructure rollout\nPUB: Sat, 16 May 2026 15:00:00 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2026/05/16/jump-crypto-s-firedancer-is-taking-a-slow-and-steady-approach-to-its-long-awaited-solana-infrastructure-rollout\nDESC: In an interview with CoinDesk, the lead engineer at Firedancer gives an update on how the new client, also known as a software, is fairing in the Solana ecosystem.\n---\nTITLE: Crypto users are choosing juicy yields over protection, putting billions at risk of hacks\nPUB: Sat, 16 May 2026 14:00:00 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/05/16/crypto-users-are-choosing-juicy-yields-over-protection-putting-billions-at-risk-of-hacks\nDESC: DeFi insurance protocols debuted with huge ambitions during the 2020 crypto boom. But as hacks evolved and users chased yields over protection, most of the sector collapsed under the same risks it was built to cover.\n---\nTITLE: XRP beat bitcoin gains as Clarity Act advanced, but a real bullrun still needs Congress\nPUB: Sat, 16 May 2026 11:30:00 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/15/xrp-beat-bitcoin-gains-as-clarity-act-advanced-but-a-real-bullrun-still-needs-congress\nDESC: The token jumped 5% after a Senate committee moved the market-structure bill forward, reviving hopes that legal clarity can pull deeper institutional money into XRP products.\n---\nTITLE: Crypto longs lose $500 million as bitcoin slides to $78,000, SOL and XRP down 5%\nPUB: Sat, 16 May 2026 07:36:02 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/16/crypto-longs-lose-usd500-million-as-bitcoin-slides-to-usd78-000-sol-and-xrp-down-5\nDESC: A long-skewed liquidation cascade flushed leverage across the major tokens overnight, with the move tracking a global bond selloff and the worst session for U.S. stocks since March.\n---\nTITLE: Bhutan ‘doesn’t recall’ selling any bitcoin, disputing widely tracked $1 billion BTC drawdown\nPUB: Sat, 16 May 2026 02:30:00 +0000\nLINK: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/16/bhutan-doesn-t-recall-selling-any-bitcoin-disputing-widely-tracked-usd1-billion-btc-drawdown\nDESC: Arkham Intelligence data shows that over $1 billion in bitcoin has left wallets attributed to Bhutan in the past year, flowing to exchanges and trading firms. The country says it has not sold any.\n---\n\n## CoinTelegraph\nTITLE: BTC price ‘bull trap’ at $76.5K? Five things to know in Bitcoin this week\nPUB: Mon, 18 May 2026 10:23:31 +0000\nLINK: https://cointelegraph.com/markets/btc-price-bull-trap-76-5k-five-things-bitcoin-this-week?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium